            "content": "### Statutory and Examination Rules for Precis Writing\n\nA Precis is an accurate, condensed miniature of the source passage preserving its entire logical core.\n\n**Essential Rules**:\n1. **Target Word Count**: Must be strictly one-third (1/3) of the total words in the source text. (e.g., Original: 450 words -> Precis: 150 words ± 10%).\n2. **Mandatory Title**: Must provide a suitable, concise title at the top summarizing the subject matter.\n3. **Candidate's Own Words**: Avoid copying verbatim sentences; rephrase ideas concisely.\n4. **Third Person & Past Tense**: Write consistently in third person ('The author observed...', 'The report highlighted...').\n5. **Absolute Objectivity**: Never insert personal opinions, commentary, criticisms, or external facts not present in the original text.\n6. **Omissions**: Completely discard rhetorical questions, repetitive analogies, direct quotations, and detailed statistical tables.\n7. **Word Count Declaration**: Always conclude with: *'Number of words in original text: X; Number of words in precis: Y.'*",
