            "content": "### Methodology for Technical Reading Comprehension in SAS\n\n1. **Two-Pass Reading Strategy**:\n   - *Pass 1 (Skimming)*: Read the passage swiftly to understand the central theme, major arguments, and logical structure.\n   - *Question Scan*: Read all 3 to 5 questions carefully to note specific target keywords and data points required.\n   - *Pass 2 (Targeted Reading)*: Locate the exact paragraphs containing the relevant information and formulate concise answers.\n2. **Precision and Brevity**:\n   - Answer only what is asked; do not introduce unrelated background knowledge.\n   - Write in complete, grammatically sound sentences.\n   - Express answers in your own words rather than copying whole sentences directly from the passage.\n3. **Distinguishing Factual from Inferential Questions**:\n   - *Factual Questions*: Require specific dates, figures, definitions, or statutory sections directly stated in the text.\n   - *Inferential Questions*: Require synthesizing the author's implied reasoning, policy justification, or logical deduction.",
