            "id": "pc2_s2_c2",
            "chapterNum": 2,
            "title": "Ethics in Audit, including CAG's Code of Ethics and ISSAI 130",
            "content": "### Code of Ethics in IA&AD and ISSAI 130\n\nThe CAG's Code of Ethics is based on ISSAI 130 and establishes mandatory ethical conduct for all audit personnel:\n\n1. **Integrity**:\n   - Auditors must act honestly, reliably, in good faith, and strictly in the public interest.\n   - Refuse any gifts, hospitality, or inducements that could compromise objectivity.\n2. **Independence, Objectivity and Impartiality**:\n   - Independent in fact and appearance.\n   - Declare conflicts of interest (personal, family, or past employment links with auditee entity).\n   - Avoid political involvement or partisan activities.\n3. **Professional Competence and Due Care**:\n   - Maintain up-to-date knowledge of auditing standards, financial rules, and IT tools.\n   - Apply due professional care, diligence, and thorough verification.\n4. **Confidentiality and Professional Secrecy**:\n   - Maintain secrecy of unpublished official records, sensitive financial data, and audit findings prior to tabling in Parliament/Legislature.\n5. **Professional Behaviour**:\n   - Maintain civil, courteous, objective, and professional relations with auditee staff during field inspections.",
