            "title": "Follow up: PAC/Legislative Committees, ATN/ATR",
            "content": "### Legislative Follow-Up: Public Accounts Committee (PAC), COPU & Action Taken Reports\n\n1. **Public Accounts Committee (PAC)**:\n   - Parliamentary/Legislative committee examining the Appropriation Accounts, Finance Accounts, and CAG Audit Reports.\n   - Examines whether money disbursed was legally available and conformed to the authority governing it.\n2. **Committee on Public Undertakings (COPU)**:\n   - Examines CAG Audit Reports on PSUs and commercial undertakings.\n3. **Role of C&AG in PAC/COPU**:\n   - The C&AG acts as the 'Friend, Philosopher, and Guide' to the PAC, briefing members on complex audit findings and evaluating departmental replies.\n4. **Action Taken Notes (ATNs) & Action Taken Reports (ATRs)**:\n   - Administrative Ministries must submit Action Taken Notes (ATNs) on audit paragraphs within 3 months of tabling.\n   - IA&AD verifies the ATNs (vetted by Audit) to ensure systemic corrective action has been implemented before PAC closes the paragraph.",
