            "content": "### Computer Networks, Network Security and Cloud Computing\n\n1. **Network Topologies and Scope**:\n   - *LAN (Local Area Network)*: High-speed connection within single office building/campus (Ethernet, Wi-Fi 6).\n   - *WAN (Wide Area Network)*: Connecting geographically dispersed offices (e.g. NICNET, IA&AD WAN, SWAN) using MPLS, leased lines, or secure VPN tunnels.\n   - *OSI 7-Layer Model*: Physical, Data Link, Network (IP), Transport (TCP/UDP), Session, Presentation, Application (HTTP, DNS, SSH).\n2. **Cloud Computing Service Models**:\n   - **IaaS (Infrastructure as a Service)**: Cloud provider supplies virtualized compute, storage, and networking (e.g. MeghRaj Cloud, AWS EC2); user manages OS, runtime, and apps.\n   - **PaaS (Platform as a Service)**: Cloud provider manages hardware, OS, and runtime; user deploys application code and data (e.g. Google App Engine, Azure App Service).\n   - **SaaS (Software as a Service)**: End-user application delivered over web; provider manages entire stack (e.g. GeM portal, SPARROW, PFMS, Office 365).\n3. **Cloud Deployment Models**: Public, Private (Government Community Cloud), Hybrid.",
