            "title": "1. Fundamental Rules & Supplementary Rules (Part I): (e) Medical Certificate of Fitness on first entry",
            "content": "### Medical Certificate of Fitness upon First Entry (FR 10)\n\n1. **Statutory Requirement (FR 10)**: No person may be appointed in India to a post in government service without producing a medical certificate of health signed by a designated medical authority.\n2. **Form and Competent Authority**: Form prescribed in Supplementary Rule 4; signed by a Civil Surgeon or District Medical Board for Gazetted/Group A & B posts, and authorized medical officer for Group C posts.\n3. **Exemptions**: Those previously medically examined for permanent government service without break, or temporary employees appointed for less than 3 months.",
