            "id": "pc4_s3_c6",
            "chapterNum": 6,
            "title": "6. Civil Accounts Manual (Revised second edition 2007) issued by CGA",
            "content": "### 6. Civil Accounts Manual (Revised 2nd edition 2007)\n\nThe **Civil Accounts Manual (CAM)**, issued by the **Controller General of Accounts (CGA)**, Department of Expenditure, Ministry of Finance, is the authoritative procedural code governing the departmentalized accounting system across all Central Civil Ministries and Departments.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Civil Accounts Organization Structure\nFollowing the separation of accounts from audit in 1976:\n- **Controller General of Accounts (CGA)**: The apex technical and administrative authority under the Ministry of Finance, responsible for prescribing accounting standards, consolidating monthly Union accounts, and overseeing the Indian Civil Accounts Service (ICAS).\n- **Principal Accounts Office (PrAO)**: Attached to each Ministry, consolidating accounts from field PAOs.\n- **Pay and Accounts Office (PAO)**: The core operational unit executing pre-check of bills, issuing cheques/e-payments, and compiling monthly classified abstracts.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Bill Passing and Pre-Check Procedures (Chapters 4 & 5)\nEvery bill submitted by a Drawing and Disbursing Officer (DDO) undergoes rigorous **pre-check** in the PAO:\n\n```\n                          PAO PRE-CHECK VERIFICATION WORKFLOW\n                                           |\n         +---------------------------------+---------------------------------+\n         |                                 |                                 |\n1. INWARD & REGISTRATION          2. TECHNICAL PRE-CHECK            3. PAYMENT & BOOKING\n- Entry in Register of Bills      - Verification of budget sanction - Bill passed and endorsed\n  Received (Form CAM-14)            in Control Register (CAM-9)       by Pay & Accounts Officer\n- Issuance of physical token      - Verification of DDO signature   - Cheque / PFMS e-payment\n  or automated digital token        against specimen signature        instruction generated\n- Strict first-come-first-        - Arithmetic accuracy checks      - Daily posting in Cheque\n  served processing priority      - Rule compliance (GFR & DFPR)      Drawing Register (CAM-17)\n```\n\n- **Important Pre-Check Scrutinies**:\n  - *Pay Bills*: Checking Last Pay Certificates (LPC), service book entries for promotions/increments, and statutory recoveries (NPS, GPF, CGEGIS, CGHS, Income Tax).\n  - *Contingent Bills*: Verifying administrative approval, financial sanction from competent authority under DFPR, and original supporting vouchers.\n  - *Advance Bills (AC Bills)*: Verifying that previous AC bills have been adjusted through Detailed Countersigned (DC) bills within the prescribed timeframe.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Compilation of Monthly Accounts: Classified Abstract (CAM-34)\n- **Daily Compilation**: Transactions are posted daily into the Compilation Sheet from passed bills and challans.\n- **Classified Abstract (Form CAM-34)**: Summarizes all receipts and disbursements for the month by Major, Minor, Sub, Detailed, and Object Heads.\n- **Monthly Account Submission**: Submitted electronically to the CGA via the **Public Financial Management System (PFMS)** portal by the **15th of the following month**, forming the basis of the monthly macroeconomic fiscal indicators of the Union Government.\n",
            "gist": "Civil Accounts Manual regulates Central Civil Accounts: separation of audit and accounts (Ch 1), PAO pre-check procedures (Ch 7-8), RBI CAS Nagpur inter-governmental adjustments (Ch 10), and pension authorisations (Ch 16-17).",
            "crux": "1. PAO performs pre-check of bills before making payment.\n2. Inter-governmental adjustments effected through RBI CAS Nagpur.\n3. CAM Appendix B governs cheque drawing DDOs and bank reconciliation.",
