            "id": "pc4_s3_c7",
            "chapterNum": 7,
            "title": "7. Central Public Works Accounts Code with Appendices",
            "content": "### 7. Central Public Works Accounts Code with Appendices\n\nThe **Central Public Works Account Code (CPWA Code)** regulates the financial and accounting transactions of the **Central Public Works Department (CPWD)**, State PWDs, Irrigation, Public Health Engineering, and other infrastructure divisions. It establishes the legal and procedural rules governing works contracts, measurement books, contractor billing, and divisional accounting.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Divisional Hierarchy and Operational Structure\n- **Chief Engineer**: Administrative head of the engineering zone.\n- **Superintending Engineer (Circle Officer)**: Administrative and technical oversight over divisions.\n- **Executive Engineer (Divisional Officer / DDO)**: In executive charge of the Division; holds drawing powers and signs works contracts.\n- **Assistant Engineer (Sub-Divisional Officer)**: In charge of a Sub-division; supervises site works.\n- **Junior Engineer (Section Officer)**: Primary field officer taking physical measurements of executed works.\n\n---\n\n### 2. The Measurement Book (MB) - Form CPWA 23\nThe **Measurement Book (MB)** is the most sacrosanct primary record in works accounting:\n- **Legal and Evidentiary Sanctity**: All measurements of work done or supplies delivered by contractors must be recorded directly in the MB. The MB serves as the sole legal basis for all payments to contractors.\n- **Strict Recording Rules**:\n  - All entries must be made **directly at the site in indelible ink**.\n  - **No Erasures or Overwriting**: If an error is made, it must be struck through with a single line and corrected above, fully initialed by the officer.\n  - No blank pages or lines may be left; unused spaces must be cancelled with diagonal lines.\n- **Mandatory Test-Check of Measurements**:\n  - The **Sub-Divisional Officer (Assistant Engineer)** must test-check at least **50 percent** of the measurements recorded by the Junior Engineer.\n  - The **Divisional Officer (Executive Engineer)** must test-check at least **10 percent** of the measurements, focusing on high-value and concealed items (e.g., foundation concrete, underground earthwork).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Contractor Billing Mechanisms\n\n```\n                         CONTRACTOR BILLING FORMS IN CPWA CODE\n                                           |\n         +---------------------------------+---------------------------------+\n         |                                 |                                 |\nFIRST & FINAL BILL (FORM CPWA 24)  RUNNING ACCOUNT BILL (CPWA 26)     FINAL BILL (FORM CPWA 27)\n- Used for small works completed   - Used for large projects          - Prepared on full completion\n  in a single measurement cycle      requiring interim payments         of the entire contract\n- Single payment upon full         - Advance payments based on        - Requires formal Completion\n  satisfactory completion            measurements to date               Certificate from EE\n- Measurements recorded in MB      - \"Secured Advances\" on non-       - Final settlement of all\n  prior to bill preparation          perishable materials at site       retention money and claims\n```\n\n- **Secured Advances**: An advance granted to a contractor on the security of imperishable materials (steel, cement) brought to the site, limited to **75 percent of the assessed market value**, subject to execution of an Indenture Bond in Form CPWA 31.\n\n---\n\n### 4. The Dual Role of the Divisional Accountant (DA)\nThe **Divisional Accountant (DA)** occupies a unique constitutional and administrative status:\n1. **Internal Auditor and Financial Adviser**: Advises the Executive Engineer on all financial matters, contract clauses, and adherence to codes.\n2. **Representative of the Accountant General**: Functions as the primary accounting agent of the AG (A&E) within the Division.\n- *Statutory Veto and Overruling*: If the Executive Engineer overrules the financial advice or audit objection of the DA, the DA must record his note of dissent in the order book, and the Executive Engineer must submit the case to the Superintending Engineer for confirmation, sending a copy to the Accountant General.\n",
            "gist": "CPWA Code governs divisional accounts: Muster Roll for labour, MB for contractor measurements, and Suspense Heads (Stock, MPWA, Workshop Suspense).",
            "crux": "1. Measurement Book (MB) is the fundamental document for works payments.\n2. MPWA: Temporary suspense head for losses, recoveries, and unadjusted advances.\n3. Divisional Accountant acts as internal auditor and financial advisor to EE.",
