            "title": "(iii) Form of the Statements, Appendices, etc. incorporated in Finance Accounts",
            "content": "### Statements and Appendices in State Finance Accounts\n\n**Two-Volume Structure**:\n1. **Volume I (Macro-level Overview)**:\n   - Statement 1: Summary of Financial Position (Assets vs Liabilities).\n   - Statement 2: Summary of Receipts and Disbursements (Consolidated Fund, Contingency Fund, Public Account).\n   - Statement 3: Summary of Expenditure (by functions - General, Social, Economic).\n   - Statement 4: Summary of Receipts (Tax, Non-tax, Central transfers).\n   - Statement 5 to 10: Public Debt, Loans & Advances, Guarantees, Investments, and Cash Balances.\n2. **Volume II (Detailed Financial Accounts)**:\n   - Statements 11 to 22: Detailed accounts of Revenue Receipts, Capital Expenditure (by minor head), Borrowings, GPF, Sinking Funds, and Suspense.\n   - Appendices: Cash balances reconciliation, investments in PSUs, salary expenditure, Centrally Sponsored Schemes fund flows.",
            "gist": "Finance Accounts Volume I contains macro Statements 1 to 10; Volume II contains detailed operational Statements 11 to 22 plus technical Appendices.",
            "crux": "1. Statement 1 summarizes overall financial assets and liabilities.\n2. Statement 9 details government guarantees given.\n3. Statement 14 details capital expenditure by minor head.",
