            "id": "pc11_s2_c2",
            "chapterNum": 2,
            "title": "(ii) Delegation of Powers in Accounting Operations",
            "content": "### (ii) Delegation of Powers in Accounting Operations\n\nIn the **Offices of the Principal Accountants General / Accountants General (Accounts & Entitlements) [PAG/AG (A&E)]**, efficiency in compiling State Civil Accounts, authorizing pension claims, and maintaining General Provident Fund (GPF) ledgers depends upon a well-defined **Delegation of Powers**. Governed by the **CAG's MSO (Administrative)**, **MSO (A&E) Volume I**, and local office manuals, this framework balances administrative decentralization with internal control and accountability.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Statutory Foundation and Operational Hierarchy\nFinancial and accounting operations within an AG (A&E) office are organized across a four-tier operational hierarchy:\n\n```\n                      ACCOUNTING HIERARCHY & DELEGATED LEVELS\n                                         |\n         +-------------------------------+-------------------------------+\n         |                                                               |\nPRINCIPAL AG / AG (HEAD OF DEPARTMENT)                            DEPUTY AG (GROUP OFFICER)\n- Overall statutory and administrative head                      - In charge of functional wings (e.g., Accounts,\n- Exercises full powers under DFPR & MSO                          Funds, Pension, Administration)\n- Final authority for annual accounts approval                   - Vets major accounting adjustments & write-offs\n\nSR. ACCOUNTS OFFICER / ACCOUNTS OFFICER (BRANCH OFFICER)          ASSISTANT ACCOUNTS OFFICER (SECTIONAL SUPERVISOR)\n- In executive charge of functional sections                     - Primary supervisory review of initial accounts\n- Passes vouchers and approves journal entries                   - Validates GPF calculations & pension service checks\n- Signs official correspondence with Treasuries/DDOs             - Supervises daily ledger postings and broadsheets\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Functional Delegation across Core Operational Wings\n1. **Treasury Accounts and Civil Accounts Compilation**:\n   - *Assistant Accounts Officer (AAO)*: Scrutinizes monthly cash accounts, treasury lists of payments, and vouchers; reviews classified abstracts; checks transfer entries (TEs).\n   - *Senior Accounts Officer (Sr. AO)*: Approves monthly classified and consolidated abstracts; authorizes correction journal entries up to prescribed financial limits; signs the Monthly Civil Account dispatch note.\n   - *Group Officer (DAG Accounts)*: Reviews and approves monthly civil accounts submitted to the State Finance Department; investigates persistent un-reconciled treasury differences.\n2. **General Provident Fund (GPF) Operations**:\n   - *AAO*: Vets final GPF withdrawal calculations; verifies title of claimants in death cases; audits annual interest computations.\n   - *Sr. AO*: Authorizes final GPF payments to retiring employees; approves transfer of GPF balances between accounting circles.\n   - *Group Officer*: Approves missing credit adjustments beyond specified monetary thresholds and handles disputed legal heirship claims.\n3. **Pension and Entitlement Processing**:\n   - *AAO*: Verifies qualifying service against service book records; checks average emoluments calculations under **CCS (Pension) Rules**.\n   - *Sr. AO*: Approves and formally signs statutory **Pension Payment Orders (PPO)**, **Gratuity Payment Orders (GPO)**, and **Commuted Pension Orders (CPO)**.\n   - *Group Officer*: Decides on complex pension cases involving disciplinary proceedings, periods of suspension, or court litigation.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Safe Custody, Token Controls and Supervisory Checks\n- **Custody of Valuables and Cheques**: Cheque books, PPO books, and valuable security registers must remain under the personal custody of designated Gazetted Officers.\n- **Segregation of Duties**: No individual compiler or officer is permitted to both initiate and authorize an accounting adjustment or payment.\n- **Mandatory Staff Rotation**: Staff handling sensitive entitlement desks (such as pension passing or GPF final settlements) must be rotated periodically (ordinarily every three years) to prevent vested interests and collusion.\n",
