            "title": "(iii) Treasury inspection in e-environment including checklist to be followed",
            "content": "### Treasury Inspection in e-Environment: CAG GA Wing Directives\n\n1. **Mandate**: Inspection of Treasuries under Section 12 of DPC Act 1971.\n2. **Post-IFMS Audit Checklist (GA Wing 2020)**:\n   - *User Credential Management*: Inactive DDO accounts, sharing of login credentials/passwords, absence of dual-factor authentication.\n   - *Token & Bill Queue*: Verification whether bills were cleared out of queue order without justification.\n   - *Cybersecurity & Network*: Unpatched operating systems, disabled antivirus on treasury workstations.\n   - *Cyber Treasury Scrutiny*: Verification of e-Receipt scrolls with bank payment gateway settlement statements.",
            "gist": "Post-IFMS treasury inspections focus on IT security: user access controls, queue management, cyber treasury reconciliations, and unauthorized bypass of budget controls.",
            "crux": "1. Governed by GA Wing Guidelines dated 22.10.2020.\n2. Verifies whether DDO credentials are shared or misused.\n3. Checks Cyber Treasury reconciliation between payment gateway and bank scrolls.",
