            "content": "### The Government Budget Formulation Cycle\n\n1. **Budget Circular**: Issued in September/October by Budget Division of Ministry of Finance / State Finance Department.\n2. **Estimates Formulation**: DDOs and administrative ministries prepare:\n   - Actuals of prior year.\n   - Budget Estimates (BE) of current year.\n   - Revised Estimates (RE) of current year based on first 6 months' trend.\n   - Budget Estimates (BE) for upcoming financial year.\n3. **Pre-Budget Discussions**: Scrutiny of departmental proposals, trimming unviable schemes.\n4. **Cabinet Approval & Printing**: Budget presented on 1st February (Union) or February/March (States).",
            "gist": "Budget formulation runs from October circular through departmental estimates (Actuals, BE, RE), finance ministry scrutiny, cabinet approval, and presentation.",
