            "content": "### Off-Budget Borrowings (OBB): Accounting Evasion & Audit Scrutiny\n\n1. **Definition of OBB**: Borrowings undertaken by State PSUs, Special Purpose Vehicles (SPVs), boards, or corporations (e.g. State Irrigation SPVs, Power Finance Corporations) on the backing of a Government Guarantee, where the debt servicing (principal repayment and interest) is financed directly or indirectly out of the Government Budget.\n2. **Modus Operandi**: Governments borrow off-budget to bypass the annual borrowing ceilings fixed under the FRBM Act and Article 293(3).\n3. **CAG Audit Treatment**: The C&AG uncovers OBB and **re-incorporates it into the State's Total Debt and Fiscal Deficit** in the State Finances Audit Report, exposing the true un-doctored deficit.",
