            "title": "1. General understanding of budgeting, expenditure, sanction, receipts, banks modules of IFMS",
            "content": "### IFMS Architecture: Module Workflows and Interdependencies\n\n1. **Integrated Modules**:\n   - *Budget Module*: Receives legislative appropriation; enforces budget ceiling on DDO bill passing.\n   - *Expenditure & Sanction Module*: Captures administrative and financial sanctions with sanction order verification.\n   - *Receipts Module (Cyber Treasury)*: Captures state tax/non-tax revenues collected via payment gateways.\n   - *Banking Interface Module*: Direct API interface with RBI e-Kuber and accredited agency banks.\n2. **Interdependency Checks**: IFMS automatically blocks bills if budget allocation is exhausted under the 15-digit classification code, preventing unauthorized overdraft.",
            "gist": "IFMS integrates Budget, Sanctions, Expenditure, Receipts, and Banking modules, enforcing automated budget checks before bills can be passed.",
            "crux": "1. Budget module prevents expenditure beyond legislative grants.\n2. Cyber Treasury reconciles e-receipts from multiple banking gateways.\n3. Banking interface enables direct settlement with RBI e-Kuber.",
