            "content": "### Treasury Process Flow and System Reports in IFMS\n\n1. **Step-by-Step Process Flow**:\n   - Step 1: DDO prepares bill online and digitally signs with DSC token.\n   - Step 2: Bill received in Treasury; system assigns automated sequential Token Number.\n   - Step 3: Assistant / Accountant verifies bill rules, vouchers, sanctions, and budget availability on Verification Screen.\n   - Step 4: Treasury Officer / Assistant Treasury Officer (ATO) authorizes payment using DSC (Maker-Checker protocol).\n   - Step 5: System generates e-Payment file pushed directly to RBI e-Kuber.\n2. **Key Treasury Reports**:\n   - *Bill Inward & Outward Register Report*.\n   - *List of Payments (LOP)*: Grouped by major heads.\n   - *Objection / Retrenchment Report*: Listing rejected bills with codal objection reasons.\n   - *Daily Cash Account & Balance Sheet*.",
            "gist": "Treasury workflow: DDO bill creation -> Automated token -> Accountant verification -> Treasury Officer DSC approval -> e-Payment file to e-Kuber.",
