            "title": "4. Understanding of data extraction and analytics tool: IDEA",
            "content": "### Audit Data Analytics Using CaseWare IDEA in Treasury Audit\n\n1. **Core Functions in Treasury Analytics**:\n   - *Duplicate Key Detection*: Spots duplicate payments with same DDO, vendor PAN, amount, or voucher date.\n   - *Gap Detection*: Identifies missing voucher numbers in sequential treasury payment schedules.\n   - *Benford's Law Analysis*: Tests the natural distribution of first digits in voucher amounts to detect manipulated accounting entries.\n   - *Stratification & Aging*: Classifies deposits in Major Head 8443 by age (unclaimed deposits > 3 years lapsing to government under GAR Rule 189).\n   - *Sampling*: Generates random samples and Monetary Unit Samples (MUS) for physical voucher audit.",
            "gist": "IDEA software executes automated analytics on treasury data: duplicate payment identification, gap detection in voucher numbers, and Benford's Law fraud testing.",
            "crux": "1. Benford's Law analysis spots artificial clustering of voucher numbers.\n2. Duplicate key extraction detects double payments to vendors.\n3. Stratification identifies un-refunded deposits older than 3 years.",
