            "content": "### Mandatory Treasury Registers and Operational Records\n\n1. **Token Register**: Logs every bill received with time stamp and sequential number.\n2. **Register of Cheques / e-Payment Register**: Logs all payment authorizations issued.\n3. **Deposit Register (Form 8443)**: Tracks Revenue Deposits, Civil Court Deposits, Earnest Money Deposits; records date of receipt, repayment, and balance.\n4. **Retrenchment / Objection Slip Register**: Records bills returned with audit objections.\n5. **Strong Room Register**: Double-lock register for safe custody of cash, judicial/non-judicial stamps, and opium.\n6. **Specimen Signature Book**: Master signature specimens of all authorized DDOs under treasury jurisdiction.",
            "gist": "Mandatory registers: Token Register, e-Payment Register, Deposit Register (8443), Objection Slip Register, Strong Room Register, and DDO Specimen Signature Book.",
            "crux": "1. Deposit Register tracks deposits lapsing to government after 3 years.\n2. Strong Room operates under mandatory double-lock custody.\n3. DDO Specimen Signature Book prevents unauthorized bill encashment.",
